'''''Dracaena hyacinthoides''''' (many authorities continue to use its synonym ''Sansevieria hyacinthoides''), called the '''African bowstring hemp''', '''Somali hemp''', '''Somali good luck plant''', '''piles root''', '''iguanatail''', and '''mother-in-law's-tongue''' (a name it shares with ''[[Dracaena trifasciata]]''), is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Asparagaceae]].<ref name="nparks_5499" >{{cite web |url=https://www.nparks.gov.sg/florafaunaweb/flora/5/4/5499 |title=''Dracaena hyacinthoides'' (L.) Mabb. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=28 March 2022 |website=nparks.gov.sg |publisher=Flora Fauna Web |access-date=1 May 2026 }}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |last1=Rojas-Sandoval |first1=Julissa |last2=Acevedo-Rodríguez |first2=Pedro |title=''Sansevieria hyacinthoides'' (African bowstring hemp) |date=2012 |journal=CABI Compendium |doi=10.1079/cabicompendium.48195 |doi-access=free }}</ref><ref name="Druce_sanbi" >{{cite web |url=https://pza.sanbi.org/sansevieria-hyacinthoides |title=''Sansevieria hyacinthoides'' (L.) Druce |last1=Mothogoane |first1=M.S. |date=January 2015 |website=pza.sanbi.org |publisher=SA National Biodiversity Institute |access-date=1 May 2026 }}</ref> It is native to eastern Africa, from Kenya to South Africa, and it has been introduced to other locales, particularly Florida, the Caribbean, and Central America.<ref name="POWO_77164234-1" >{{cite POWO |id=77164234-1 |title=''Dracaena hyacinthoides'' (L.) Mabb. |access-date=1 May 2026 }}</ref><ref name="Invasive_6357" >{{cite web |url=https://www.invasiveplantatlas.org/subject.html?sub=6357 |title=iguanatail ''Sansevieria hyacinthoides'' (L.) Druce |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=October 2018 |website=invasiveplantatlas.org |publisher=Invasive Plant Atlas of the United States |access-date=1 May 2026 }}</ref> An erect shrub reaching {{cvt|0.9|m|ft|0}}, it is found in the seasonally dry tropics.<ref name="POWO_77164234-1" /><ref name="FNA_242101879" >{{cite web |url=http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=1&taxon_id=242101879 |title=1. ''Sansevieria hyacinthoides'' (Linnaeus) Druce, Rep. Bot. Exch. Club. 3: 423. 1914. African bowstring hemp |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2026 |website=Flora of North America |publisher=Missouri Botanical Garden & Harvard University Herbaria |access-date=1 May 2026 }}</ref>

==Uses==
''Dracaena hyacinthoides'' is used as an ornamental in warm areas and as a houseplant, performing best in semi-shade.<ref name="nparks_5499" /> As some of its common names suggest, it is a minor fiber crop, and in its home range it is used as a treatment for [[hemorrhoid]]s.<ref name="Druce_sanbi" /><ref>{{cite web |url=https://tropical.theferns.info/viewtropical.php?id=Sansevieria+hyacinthoides |title=Useful Tropical Plants ''Sansevieria hyacinthoides'' |last1=Fern |first1=Ken |date=13 October 2024 |website=tropical.theferns.info |publisher=Tropical Plants Database |access-date=2 August 2023 }}</ref>
